{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The value of a certain fishing boat was <math alttext=\"dollar sign 24,000\"><mo>$</mo><mn>24,000</mn></math> when it was purchased. Each year, the value of the fishing boat decreased by <math alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the previous year&rsquo;s value. Which equation represents this situation, where <math alttext=\"v\"><mi>v</mi>\n</math><em>&nbsp;</em>is the value of the fishing boat, in dollars, and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is the number of years since the fishing boat was purchased?</p>", "keys": ["46dbb311-9af8-47dc-a07d-06b164b35c6a"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "51046f9f-dd5a-48f4-a3e3-e510827564e0", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"v equals 0.8 left parenthesis 24,000 right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>24,000</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>y</mi></msup></math></p>"}, {"id": "d46bcb29-80a5-408c-9ec7-3cb0c7c85e46", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"v equals 1.2 left parenthesis 24,000 right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>24,000</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>y</mi></msup></math></p>"}, {"id": "46dbb311-9af8-47dc-a07d-06b164b35c6a", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"v equals 24,000 left parenthesis 0.8 right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24,000</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0.8</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>y</mi></msup></math></p>"}, {"id": "6be73b87-67e1-44a5-8422-13378f381b46", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"v equals 24,000 left parenthesis 1.2 right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24,000</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>1.2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>y</mi></msup></math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the value of a certain fishing boat was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"dollar sign 24,000\"><mo>$</mo><mn>24,000</mn></math> when it was purchased. It's also given that each year, the value of the fishing boat decreased by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the previous year's value. It follows that this situation can be represented by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v equals a left parenthesis 1 minus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v\"><mi>v</mi></math> is the value of the boat, in dollars,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> years since it was purchased,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is the value of the boat, in dollars, when it was purchased, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the percent by which the value of the boat decreases each year from the previous year's value. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24,000\"><mn>24,000</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v equals 24,000 left parenthesis 1 minus StartFraction 20 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24,000</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v equals 24,000 left parenthesis 0.8 right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24,000</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.8</mn></mfenced><mi>y</mi></msup></math>. Therefore,&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v equals 24,000 left parenthesis 0.8 right parenthesis Superscript y\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24,000</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.8</mn></mfenced><mi>y</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;represents this situation.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a situation where each year the value of the boat increased, not decreased, by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the previous year's value.</p>", "externalid": "a598add1-606e-453f-8b43-02083a30f5c7", "correct_answer": ["C"]}